WEBVTT

00:08.259 --> 00:10.218
- I'm leaving town.
- I'll be damned.

00:10.219 --> 00:11.886
It's Cat, isn't it?

00:11.887 --> 00:13.888
I'm really happy for you.

00:13.889 --> 00:14.931
I know about Winston.

00:14.932 --> 00:16.099
I know you set him up,

00:16.100 --> 00:17.392
and I know you did it for her.

00:17.393 --> 00:18.685
I didn't tell the boss 'cause

00:18.686 --> 00:20.061
he would've killed the both of you.

00:20.062 --> 00:23.440
Every four years,
I decide who sits in that chair.

00:23.441 --> 00:26.359
You just move on to the next guy
and expect me to go quietly?

00:26.360 --> 00:27.777
My mutation is aging me

00:27.778 --> 00:29.404
at a dog's clip.

00:29.405 --> 00:30.655
Dr. Faber is

00:30.656 --> 00:33.158
my last chance to survive.

00:33.159 --> 00:35.285
- Where am I?
-  My private laboratory.

00:35.286 --> 00:37.036
This will all be a lot easier

00:37.037 --> 00:38.705
if you calm down and let me do my work.

00:38.706 --> 00:41.541
I believe that
whatever process that allowed

00:41.542 --> 00:44.043
the mutation to stabilize within your body

00:44.044 --> 00:45.754
can be retrofitted

00:45.755 --> 00:48.339
to fully cure the other mutations.

00:48.340 --> 00:50.425
Oh!

00:50.426 --> 00:51.634
She's quite beautiful,

00:51.635 --> 00:53.303
the one who told me how to find you.

00:53.304 --> 00:54.304
Cat.

00:54.305 --> 00:56.848
I'm curious to know
if there are others like them.

00:56.849 --> 00:59.893
- My God.
- These men was our comrades.

01:01.645 --> 01:03.188
Nothing here for us.

01:03.189 --> 01:04.898
Would you want to be cured?

01:04.899 --> 01:06.649
The Spider was never a hero.

01:06.650 --> 01:08.693
I only did it for the thrill.

01:08.694 --> 01:10.320
Maybe you weren't then,

01:10.321 --> 01:13.365
but there's still time
for you to become one.

01:30.216 --> 01:32.258
-  Flint, please.
-  Stay away!

01:46.482 --> 01:48.483
What's left for us here?

01:48.484 --> 01:50.944
Ruby's gone, Flint's past helping.

01:50.945 --> 01:52.279
We're chasing ghosts.

01:53.697 --> 01:55.074
But you and I could have something.

01:55.783 --> 01:56.659
If I tell you...

01:57.701 --> 01:59.369
...do you promise you won't hurt him?

02:10.130 --> 02:11.257
I need a drink.

02:12.842 --> 02:14.176
Lo, the irony.

02:15.177 --> 02:19.055
A man controls the flow of alcohol
for a city of seven million souls

02:19.056 --> 02:22.685
and yet, my throat is as dry
as a camel's hole in a sandstorm.

02:23.978 --> 02:25.812
What happened at the lab?

02:25.813 --> 02:27.355
Find anything interesting?

02:27.356 --> 02:28.481
Yeah.

02:28.482 --> 02:29.899
A lot of dead soldiers.

02:29.900 --> 02:31.443
Some of them old friends.

02:34.780 --> 02:37.741
The good doctor was
making freaks in her basement.

02:38.450 --> 02:40.494
Goddamn abomination, if you ask me.

02:43.330 --> 02:44.832
That's all?

02:46.417 --> 02:49.794
She had nothing
but a bunch of meat in big jars,

02:49.795 --> 02:51.171
so we burnt the place down.

02:52.256 --> 02:53.965
You burned the place down?

02:53.966 --> 02:55.675
To the goddamn ground.

02:55.676 --> 02:57.261
What do you care?

03:01.390 --> 03:02.932
You're right.

03:02.933 --> 03:05.852
Why would I care about
a mad scientist killing veterans?

03:05.853 --> 03:08.563
I'm just a pretty girl
who likes to sing and dance.

03:08.564 --> 03:10.023
Well, I often wish you were.

03:10.024 --> 03:12.526
No, you don't. You'd have been
bored of me after six months.

03:17.781 --> 03:19.490
Another round?

03:19.491 --> 03:21.368
Does the king ride his sister?

03:26.040 --> 03:27.457
What's the point?

03:27.458 --> 03:31.002
You drink the best whiskey,
drive the best car,

03:31.003 --> 03:32.338
own the best club.

03:33.339 --> 03:34.757
What are you fighting for?

03:35.633 --> 03:37.843
The fighting is the point.

03:39.803 --> 03:41.931
It's what gives the whiskey its taste.

03:43.140 --> 03:45.059
Gives the club its danger.

03:46.060 --> 03:50.104
If anything, I owe the mayor
a debt of gratitude.

03:50.105 --> 03:53.442
I'll be sure to send flowers
to his grave when I bury the bastard.

03:56.278 --> 03:58.488
But you boys have work to do.

03:58.489 --> 04:00.156
With the doctor out of the picture,

04:00.157 --> 04:01.741
we know the score.
It's the three of you

04:01.742 --> 04:03.326
to the mayor's one.

04:03.327 --> 04:06.287
So go forth and maraud.

04:06.288 --> 04:08.289
Make some mischief and mayhem.

04:08.290 --> 04:10.375
Raid the mayor's piggy bank.

04:10.376 --> 04:11.668
Buy voters for Hudson.

04:11.669 --> 04:15.546
It's time to show that prick
of a politician who's really in charge.

04:20.928 --> 04:22.887
You love it, you know you do.

04:33.857 --> 04:36.526
♪ The colors fading from the photograph ♪

04:36.527 --> 04:38.277
♪ I could tell the story ♪

04:38.278 --> 04:40.947
♪ but still you wouldn't know the half ♪

04:40.948 --> 04:43.741
♪ This love was brought to life
from shards of glass ♪

04:43.742 --> 04:45.827
♪ When you kiss me there's a shifting ♪

04:45.828 --> 04:48.287
♪ in the sepia tone ♪

04:48.288 --> 04:51.499
♪ Can't escape the madness,
baby, magnetism ♪

04:51.500 --> 04:54.836
♪ Run away but something
pulls me back into it ♪

04:54.837 --> 04:57.964
♪ Lately I've been staring
at a broken mirror ♪

04:57.965 --> 05:01.426
♪ Needing someone to call my own ♪

05:01.427 --> 05:04.637
♪ Hey, lover ♪

05:04.638 --> 05:07.515
♪ I need someone to save me now ♪

05:07.516 --> 05:09.767
♪ from all the pain ♪

05:09.768 --> 05:12.228
♪ I suffer ♪

05:12.229 --> 05:15.064
♪ and the heavy world
that weighs me down ♪

05:15.065 --> 05:18.609
♪ 'Cause the world ain't sweet ♪

05:18.610 --> 05:20.987
♪ It's bitter to taste ♪

05:20.988 --> 05:22.363
♪ But you could be ♪

05:22.364 --> 05:25.576
♪ my saving grace ♪

06:04.907 --> 06:07.116
Dah, dah, dah, dah...

06:07.117 --> 06:10.746
You see, now, this...
this is a nice establishment.

06:14.833 --> 06:18.669
Oh, no. Oh, no, it's the boys in blue.

06:18.670 --> 06:20.214
Oh, no.

06:21.757 --> 06:23.967
Hey, you seeing this shit?

06:26.303 --> 06:27.386
Now, folks,

06:27.387 --> 06:28.971
usually I would apologize

06:28.972 --> 06:31.182
for such a disturbance,

06:31.183 --> 06:34.018
but this is most likely the greatest day

06:34.019 --> 06:37.439
of your pathetic
and miserable little lives.

06:40.359 --> 06:42.735
What? No applause?

06:42.736 --> 06:44.238
Mm.

06:51.453 --> 06:52.996
Are you the one in charge?

06:57.334 --> 06:58.794
Anybody home?

07:01.004 --> 07:04.006
Mr. Noble is the head of this office,

07:04.007 --> 07:06.008
but I can help you with whatever you need.

07:06.009 --> 07:07.426
Mm.

07:07.427 --> 07:09.720
I'm sure you can, honey.

07:09.721 --> 07:12.141
- Hey.
- Hey, relax.

07:12.933 --> 07:15.101
We're just getting into character.

07:15.102 --> 07:17.103
- Ain't that right...
- Alice.

07:17.104 --> 07:19.063
- ...Alice.
- And you don't scare me.

07:19.064 --> 07:20.064
Well, I should.

07:20.065 --> 07:20.983
- Back off.
- Oh.

07:23.485 --> 07:24.736
Okay, Alice.

07:25.737 --> 07:28.239
Now, if you wouldn't mind showing us
where the mayor keeps all his dough,

07:28.240 --> 07:29.950
that would be much appreciated.

07:34.788 --> 07:37.206
God, I want
some free time, fellas. Let's go.

07:37.207 --> 07:39.041
Hey, Alice, you know the deal.

07:39.042 --> 07:40.543
Nobody's supposed to be back--

07:40.544 --> 07:42.837
Don't blame Alice. This was our idea.

07:45.257 --> 07:47.258
Oh, lookee, lookee.

07:47.259 --> 07:50.094
You don't mind if we take
some of these things, do you?

07:50.095 --> 07:52.555
No? Good.

07:52.556 --> 07:55.016
We're gonna spread the wealth
to the people of New York.

07:55.017 --> 07:57.186
Hey, Dirk. Let's go to work.

07:58.270 --> 08:01.480
Oh, and, um, when you see him,

08:01.481 --> 08:03.900
tell our illustrious friend Morris...

08:03.901 --> 08:07.196
tell him Silvermane sends his regards.

08:10.032 --> 08:11.658
Thank you very much.

08:13.577 --> 08:14.786
Bye-bye.

08:17.497 --> 08:19.249
Are you scared?

08:20.250 --> 08:21.709
Yes, you are.

08:27.299 --> 08:29.968
Come in.

08:32.054 --> 08:33.930
You took my boss and my business.

08:33.931 --> 08:35.140
What'd you forget?

08:36.767 --> 08:38.851
I'm just messing around.

08:38.852 --> 08:41.313
I'm happy for both of you. Genuinely.

08:43.732 --> 08:45.651
- What's wrong?
- Have you seen him?

08:46.735 --> 08:48.861
What do you-- what do you mean?
He's meant to be with you.

08:48.862 --> 08:50.863
- He never showed.
- What?

08:50.864 --> 08:52.491
It's been days.

08:53.742 --> 08:56.453
And you're only just now looking for him?

08:57.454 --> 08:58.996
Well, I don't know how it is with you,

08:58.997 --> 09:00.665
but when men stand me up,
I don't usually go--

09:00.666 --> 09:02.626
Oh, God, uh, yeah. Say less.

09:05.712 --> 09:07.630
You want a drink?

09:07.631 --> 09:09.507
There's probably a bottle
still floating around somewhere.

09:09.508 --> 09:10.842
No, thank you.

09:13.845 --> 09:15.596
When was the last time
you heard from him?

09:15.597 --> 09:18.724
Uh, Saturday afternoon.

09:18.725 --> 09:21.519
He showed up
with an envelope full of cash.

09:21.520 --> 09:23.272
- That's...
- What?

09:25.649 --> 09:27.275
It's just, uh...

09:27.276 --> 09:29.443
Ben's not exactly loose with his money.

09:29.444 --> 09:31.279
Are you saying he's frugal?

09:31.280 --> 09:34.031
I'm saying it's not like him
to dump a fistful of cash on my lap

09:34.032 --> 09:35.449
unless he really thought it through.

09:35.450 --> 09:38.328
Well, men get cold feet.

09:40.539 --> 09:41.873
No.

09:42.874 --> 09:45.502
No, you wouldn't be here
if that's what you thought was going on.

09:46.586 --> 09:48.005
You're too proud for that.

09:49.131 --> 09:51.215
So, who is it?

09:51.216 --> 09:52.842
Silvermane?

09:52.843 --> 09:54.385
Morris?

09:54.386 --> 09:56.846
The doctor?
Stop me anytime if I'm getting warm.

09:56.847 --> 10:00.267
Your hand's on the stove,
but I don't know any more than that.

10:05.230 --> 10:07.481
The Daily Bugle, please.

10:07.482 --> 10:09.067
Robbie Robertson.

10:10.319 --> 10:13.113
And he didn't call or leave word
in any way, shape or form?

10:14.114 --> 10:16.574
Yes, tell him Janet called.
He'll know how to reach me.

10:16.575 --> 10:18.784
Okay, thanks.

10:25.542 --> 10:27.376
Listen, he's like a cat--

10:27.377 --> 10:30.296
If you hear anything,
you can reach me at The Alcove.

10:30.297 --> 10:31.464
Okay.

10:31.465 --> 10:33.425
- Thank you.
- Sure.

10:43.143 --> 10:45.145
Damn it, Ben, where are you?

10:46.688 --> 10:48.481
Daily Bugle, please.

10:57.407 --> 11:01.077
You know anything about
spider muscles, Eamon?

11:01.078 --> 11:02.287
No.

11:03.288 --> 11:05.207
Eh, that's because they don't have any.

11:05.707 --> 11:07.458
They're on a hydraulic system,

11:07.459 --> 11:10.836
shooting fluid to move their legs,
as it were.

11:10.837 --> 11:14.507
Their appendages are rather like straws.

11:14.508 --> 11:16.426
Veritable party whistles!

11:19.930 --> 11:21.680
But she didn't love me.

11:21.681 --> 11:22.808
That's okay.

11:23.934 --> 11:25.684
Nobody has to love anybody.

11:25.685 --> 11:28.813
But to go behind my back like that?

11:28.814 --> 11:31.565
With the doctor. What the hell was that?

11:31.566 --> 11:34.110
I mean, that's worse than a betrayal,

11:34.111 --> 11:37.613
That's adding insult to injury.

11:37.614 --> 11:39.366
Mm.

11:40.367 --> 11:43.119
But Eamon, I digress,

11:43.120 --> 11:45.955
because right here
in the palm of my hand,

11:45.956 --> 11:47.873
I hold the antidote...

11:47.874 --> 11:49.917
...to all of my problems.

11:49.918 --> 11:52.878
Yeah, well, you ain't the first one
to figure that one out, pal.

11:52.879 --> 11:54.630
It's kind of how we stay in business.

11:54.631 --> 11:57.049
Keep 'em coming, Eamon.

12:00.220 --> 12:01.471
There you go.

12:18.113 --> 12:21.450
They're using my campaign money
to fund my goddamn opponent.

12:22.993 --> 12:26.454
Please, help-help me to understand

12:26.455 --> 12:28.080
how a thing like this can happen.

12:28.081 --> 12:30.332
I mean, it-it could be something,
anything,

12:30.333 --> 12:33.711
a-anything that enlightens me
as to how it is

12:33.712 --> 12:36.922
that you're letting Silvermane
run roughshod all over my city.

12:36.923 --> 12:39.592
You mean, other than the fact
that he's got three guys on his side

12:39.593 --> 12:43.220
that can't be subdued by ordinary means?

12:43.221 --> 12:45.598
Two of my cops tried
and got electrocuted.

12:45.599 --> 12:49.269
Does that enlighten you, Mayor?

12:50.854 --> 12:52.688
Fine. You know what?

12:52.689 --> 12:54.899
It's done, that's in the past.

12:54.900 --> 12:58.777
But what I want to know
is what you plan on doing about it now.

12:58.778 --> 13:02.490
You're the goddamn chief of police.

13:02.491 --> 13:05.868
And if you can't fix this,
I will find someone who can.

13:05.869 --> 13:08.037
Frankly, Mayor,

13:08.038 --> 13:10.331
I don't think you're gonna be
in the position much longer

13:10.332 --> 13:11.750
to do anything about it.

13:15.295 --> 13:17.088
Are you threatening me?

13:18.089 --> 13:20.175
Take it however you like.

13:21.176 --> 13:22.761
But without The Spider...

13:23.553 --> 13:27.640
...you're a three-legged horse
running in quicksand.

13:27.641 --> 13:30.100
If he's such a good friend of yours,

13:30.101 --> 13:32.311
now's the time to ring him up.

13:42.697 --> 13:44.573
Come on, come on.

13:44.574 --> 13:46.116
Oh!

13:46.117 --> 13:48.077
- That was intense.
- That was wild.

13:48.078 --> 13:49.954
- How much did we get?
-  At least a hundred. Maybe two.

13:49.955 --> 13:51.581
Look at this.

13:52.541 --> 13:53.791
Should I even ask?

13:53.792 --> 13:56.001
- Nope.
- Ah, you should've seen it, Eamon.

13:56.002 --> 13:58.295
Two of them supers were
standing on the corner,

13:58.296 --> 13:59.463
throwing them in the air.

13:59.464 --> 14:01.048
"Vote for Hudson,"
they're shouting.

14:01.049 --> 14:03.300
"Vote for Hudson."
Fella, you keep chucking bills in the air,

14:03.301 --> 14:05.010
I'm gonna vote for the devil himself.

14:05.011 --> 14:06.554
They ripped off
Morris's campaign war chest,

14:06.555 --> 14:08.013
and not a cop in sight.

14:08.014 --> 14:10.307
- What about The Spider?
-  The Spider?

14:10.308 --> 14:11.684
Yeah, right.

14:11.685 --> 14:13.519
Let's not hold our breath
for that one.

14:15.230 --> 14:17.398
What the hell is that supposed to mean?

14:17.399 --> 14:19.567
I mean, have you seen him?

14:19.568 --> 14:21.777
He looks like my mom
after ten loads of laundry.

14:21.778 --> 14:23.320
I don't know
what he's been up to

14:23.321 --> 14:25.322
for the past half a decade, but the years

14:25.323 --> 14:27.074
haven't been good to him,
I'll tell you that much.

14:27.075 --> 14:28.659
Eh, he wasn't
that great to begin with.

14:28.660 --> 14:30.077
Well, I didn't miss him.

14:30.078 --> 14:31.912
He probably
just came back to, uh, you know,

14:31.913 --> 14:33.622
get his picture in the papers again.

14:33.623 --> 14:35.207
Yeah, he never missed a photo op,
that's for sure.

14:35.208 --> 14:37.501
That guy loves the spotlight
more than Morris.

14:37.502 --> 14:40.087
He may have missed
the spotlight, but he didn't miss a meal.

14:40.088 --> 14:44.675
Maybe, maybe, maybe, maybe
The Spider is a guy like anyone else.

14:44.676 --> 14:46.760
You ever think about that?

14:46.761 --> 14:48.971
You ever wonder what his problems were?

14:48.972 --> 14:51.515
He's swinging around burning buildings,
saving people,

14:51.516 --> 14:54.393
do you ever think he feels the heat?

14:54.394 --> 14:56.312
Or gets sad?

14:56.313 --> 14:57.813
Or tired?

14:57.814 --> 14:59.523
Or lonely?

15:06.698 --> 15:09.241
Geez, Eamon,
where the hell'd you find this guy?

15:09.242 --> 15:10.576
Oh, woe is me,

15:10.577 --> 15:14.079
I'm The Spider, life is so hard.

15:14.080 --> 15:16.415
Oh, look at me
in my little mask.

15:16.416 --> 15:18.917
Hey, Mommy,
I'm a big boy Spider...

15:53.536 --> 15:55.829
Hey, you're-you're The Spider.

15:55.830 --> 15:59.625
♪ When marimba rhythms start to play ♪

15:59.626 --> 16:03.296
♪ dance with me, make me sway ♪

16:04.297 --> 16:08.092
♪ Like a lazy ocean hugs the shore ♪

16:08.093 --> 16:11.387
♪ hold me close, sway me more...

16:11.388 --> 16:12.596
You like that, huh?

16:12.597 --> 16:14.390
- Huh?
- ♪ Like a flower ♪

16:14.391 --> 16:16.558
♪ bending in the breeze ♪

16:16.559 --> 16:21.188
♪ bend with me, sway with ease ♪

16:21.189 --> 16:24.692
♪ When we dance, you have a way with me ♪

16:24.693 --> 16:28.947
♪ Stay with me, sway with me ♪

16:29.948 --> 16:32.199
♪ Other dancers may be on the floor...

16:32.200 --> 16:34.118
Hey! Hey!

16:34.119 --> 16:37.996
♪ Dear, but my eyes will see only you ♪

16:37.997 --> 16:41.875
♪ Only you have the magic technique ♪

16:41.876 --> 16:43.919
♪ When we sway, I go-- ♪

16:46.339 --> 16:48.132
- ♪ Sway me smooth, sway me now...
-  They're pummeling him!

16:48.133 --> 16:50.300
Oh, yes, they... yes, pummeling it.

16:50.301 --> 16:53.972
You've got to wonder if they left
something in the tank for today.

16:57.350 --> 16:59.435
♪ Oh, I can hear the sound ♪

16:59.436 --> 17:01.478
- ♪ of violins ♪
-  Web!

17:01.479 --> 17:03.856
- Web! Web!
- ♪ long before ♪

17:03.857 --> 17:05.691
- Web! Web! Web! Web! Web!
- ♪ it begins ♪

17:05.692 --> 17:07.025
♪ Sway me smooth ♪

17:07.026 --> 17:08.778
♪ sway me now ♪

17:26.921 --> 17:28.839
Ha! Ha-cha-cha!

17:30.425 --> 17:32.426
Did you see that?

17:32.427 --> 17:34.303
They kicked him and they K'd him.

17:34.304 --> 17:35.847
Come on... oh!

17:37.807 --> 17:39.099
That one's on the house, pal.

17:39.100 --> 17:42.019
To the victor go the spoils, right?

17:42.020 --> 17:44.062
Amazing.

17:48.026 --> 17:49.526
Oh, shit.

17:49.527 --> 17:51.570
What the hell are you doing?

17:51.571 --> 17:53.615
Janet's got me looking
all over the city for you.

17:56.326 --> 17:58.577
I'm drinking. What's it look like?

17:58.578 --> 18:01.330
Come on, let's go.
You shouldn't be in here like this.

18:01.331 --> 18:04.249
Well, you don't want The Spider here,

18:04.250 --> 18:06.794
they don't want The Spider,
and guess what?

18:06.795 --> 18:09.671
I don't want The Spider anywhere.

18:09.672 --> 18:13.008
But do you know what? I can remedy that.

18:14.969 --> 18:16.386
What is that?

18:16.387 --> 18:20.349
It's a little concoction Faber cooked up.

18:20.350 --> 18:23.811
Turns supers
into run-of-the-mill schmucks.

18:23.812 --> 18:25.522
Like these clowns.

18:29.025 --> 18:31.485
- What the hell are you doing?
- Curing myself.

18:31.486 --> 18:33.153
- Oh, the hell you are.
- Hey!

18:33.154 --> 18:35.364
- Give it back.
- No.

18:35.365 --> 18:38.200
Give it back, Robbie, now.

18:38.201 --> 18:39.202
No.

18:40.328 --> 18:42.621
And I know that even
in the state that you're in,

18:42.622 --> 18:45.624
if you felt right about drinking this,

18:45.625 --> 18:47.585
you would have taken it from me
and finished it by now.

18:49.003 --> 18:52.173
All right. All right, all right,
all right, all right.

18:53.675 --> 18:54.968
Let's go.

18:58.012 --> 19:01.723
And so, the Lady Judas

19:01.724 --> 19:03.476
betrayed me.

19:04.978 --> 19:07.063
Aw, that's a tough one, man. I'm sorry.

19:09.607 --> 19:11.234
What about everyone else?

19:12.235 --> 19:13.862
What everyone else?

19:14.946 --> 19:16.865
The rest of New York.

19:17.907 --> 19:20.117
You fell for a woman
and she didn't fall back.

19:20.118 --> 19:22.369
Not sure why that means
that the whole city

19:22.370 --> 19:24.246
should lose the one guy
who can help them.

19:24.247 --> 19:26.456
Why should I care?

19:26.457 --> 19:28.626
I risked my life for them
for years, and...

19:29.752 --> 19:33.171
the second I don't do
exactly what they say,

19:33.172 --> 19:35.090
they hate me for it.

19:35.091 --> 19:36.926
I never hated you for it.

19:38.595 --> 19:40.387
When you quit, I lost everything.

19:40.388 --> 19:42.181
And I never asked you to come back.

19:43.182 --> 19:44.850
'Cause, see, you were my friend,
and I understood

19:44.851 --> 19:46.978
the price you were paying to be a hero.

19:48.771 --> 19:51.523
Maybe I had it all wrong. Maybe...

19:51.524 --> 19:53.567
you did it to be praised.

19:53.568 --> 19:56.028
Some hero. I am so impressed.

19:56.029 --> 19:59.990
I-I d... I didn't do it to be a hero.

19:59.991 --> 20:03.368
I did it because, at the time,

20:03.369 --> 20:06.330
it made me feel good,
but it doesn't anymore, okay?

20:06.331 --> 20:10.876
Well, then, maybe you should think
about why it made you feel good.

20:10.877 --> 20:12.586
And then answer this question:

20:12.587 --> 20:15.964
will you sleep better if you take
the antidote after having done nothing

20:15.965 --> 20:19.719
or if you take it
after you've helped cure Lonnie and Flint?

20:20.720 --> 20:23.180
You see, those men are soldiers,
just like you.

20:23.181 --> 20:25.557
Men who are suffering just like you.

20:26.684 --> 20:29.854
But unlike you, those men are gonna die.

20:31.564 --> 20:34.650
So, what makes you deserve this antidote
any more than they do?

20:34.651 --> 20:37.987
And what makes your life more important
than those assholes at the bar?

20:39.989 --> 20:42.825
There's a blood feud going on
between Silvermane and Morris.

20:43.826 --> 20:45.161
People are gonna die.

20:46.162 --> 20:47.579
But I guess they're not worth saving

20:47.580 --> 20:51.584
because they don't make you
feel good anymore.

20:54.754 --> 20:56.922
So, if you're gonna take this
just to be the same Ben

20:56.923 --> 20:59.926
you've been for the past five years,
then I'll be honest...

21:01.469 --> 21:02.971
...I don't really want
to be around for that.

21:03.763 --> 21:05.514
Oh, come on.

21:05.515 --> 21:07.933
You've been in a hole
ever since Ruby died,

21:07.934 --> 21:09.768
and you've never stopped digging.

21:09.769 --> 21:12.939
This is your chance
to put that shovel down.

21:15.024 --> 21:17.318
You couldn't save Ruby
because you didn't know.

21:18.027 --> 21:20.488
This time, you have a choice.

21:21.489 --> 21:23.366
You just have to make it.

21:32.083 --> 21:34.459
Here we go.

21:34.460 --> 21:36.461
Oh, my God, where have you been?

21:36.462 --> 21:38.463
- He's drunk.
- And looks like shit.

21:38.464 --> 21:40.048
I know.

21:40.049 --> 21:41.050
Wait.

21:42.176 --> 21:43.553
Are you yellow?

21:44.429 --> 21:47.055
What do you mean, "yellow"?
You mean like a, like a coward?

21:47.056 --> 21:49.516
No, like a banana.
What the hell happened to him?

21:49.517 --> 21:51.102
Well you see, Janet...

21:51.686 --> 21:53.854
...first, Cat double-crossed me,

21:53.855 --> 21:56.273
then an old man named Ogden drugged me

21:56.274 --> 21:59.985
and took me to see Dr. Faber,
who sliced me open and cut up my guts.

21:59.986 --> 22:01.319
Oh, and the old man

22:01.320 --> 22:04.322
was actually Faber's son,
but she cured him.

22:04.323 --> 22:07.034
M-Made him young again.

22:07.035 --> 22:09.995
Then Silvermane and his goons turned up,

22:09.996 --> 22:12.456
I escaped, they torched the laboratory

22:12.457 --> 22:15.000
and I got plastered.

22:15.001 --> 22:16.376
And you beat up some guys in a bar.

22:16.377 --> 22:17.586
And I beat up

22:17.587 --> 22:19.047
some guys in a bar.

22:19.881 --> 22:21.506
Why did Faber kidnap Ben?

22:21.507 --> 22:23.843
Uh, because I'm The Spider.

22:27.597 --> 22:30.849
Oopsie-poopsie,
I shouldn't have told you that.

22:30.850 --> 22:33.268
You already did tell me that.

22:36.689 --> 22:38.523
¡Ay, hijo de tu madre!

22:38.524 --> 22:40.193
I'm The Spider, Janet.

22:41.444 --> 22:43.070
I Spider.

22:43.071 --> 22:45.113
♪ Nice work if you can get it...

22:47.325 --> 22:49.910
The Spider's busy, Janet.

22:49.911 --> 22:52.288
Can't you see that The Spider is busy?

22:53.164 --> 22:55.457
Okay.

22:55.458 --> 22:57.959
♪ Loving one who loves you ♪

22:57.960 --> 22:59.920
♪ and then taking that vow...

23:01.506 --> 23:02.756
♪ Nice work...

23:02.757 --> 23:04.883
♪ I'm your Spider ♪

23:04.884 --> 23:07.219
♪ Be my Spider ♪

23:07.220 --> 23:09.180
♪ to be real ♪

23:13.643 --> 23:15.561
You knew?

23:17.271 --> 23:19.648
And you knew that she knew?

23:19.649 --> 23:21.483
What, you're gonna get mad
about us keeping secrets?

23:21.484 --> 23:26.114
Well, maybe you should've
told me that.

23:27.240 --> 23:29.199
I figured you'd worry less

23:29.200 --> 23:31.284
if you didn't know I knew.

23:31.285 --> 23:34.412
Plus, it's not like
you've been very Spidery lately.

23:42.171 --> 23:44.006
What's that for?

23:57.937 --> 24:00.439
You were wearing this
the first time I saw you.

24:01.941 --> 24:03.776
Can't believe you remember that.

24:05.403 --> 24:07.237
I remember a lot of things.

24:07.238 --> 24:10.073
Well, do you remember
how shy you were at first?

24:10.074 --> 24:12.450
How it took you a year
just to say hello to me?

24:12.451 --> 24:14.411
Oh, I wasn't shy.

24:14.412 --> 24:15.912
I was scared.

24:17.790 --> 24:21.418
There wasn't a single German in the war
who scared me as much as you did.

24:23.045 --> 24:25.714
- That's ridiculous.
- No, it's the truth.

24:25.715 --> 24:28.509
Before you, I didn't think women
like you even existed.

24:30.261 --> 24:31.887
Tell me more.

24:31.888 --> 24:32.889
Ah...

24:35.099 --> 24:36.517
I don't know.

24:38.519 --> 24:40.854
You know, beautiful women,
you see them around.

24:40.855 --> 24:43.857
Smart women, too. Tough ones.

24:43.858 --> 24:45.483
Talented ones.

24:45.484 --> 24:48.403
Classy, sexy, funny.

24:48.404 --> 24:50.071
Confident.

24:50.072 --> 24:51.490
Determined.

24:53.701 --> 24:56.037
But all of it all at once? It...

24:57.038 --> 24:59.831
I didn't think that would ever happen.

24:59.832 --> 25:01.250
And then there you were.

25:02.126 --> 25:04.462
And then, for you to pick me
out of all the men in the world...

25:05.546 --> 25:09.382
...for you to see something in me
that I couldn't even see in myself, I...

25:09.383 --> 25:11.886
And do you know why I let you in?

25:14.847 --> 25:16.181
I don't know.

25:16.182 --> 25:17.390
Because...

25:17.391 --> 25:20.019
anyone could see the good in me.

25:21.020 --> 25:24.147
But you knew I could also be mean,

25:24.148 --> 25:27.317
and angry and cold.

25:27.318 --> 25:30.362
You loved me at my worst,

25:30.363 --> 25:33.074
and you pushed me to be better.

25:34.867 --> 25:36.326
I love you.

25:36.327 --> 25:38.955
Why can't you get that through your head?

25:39.956 --> 25:41.374
Don't you get it?

25:43.000 --> 25:44.418
I do believe you.

25:45.419 --> 25:47.504
But there's no coming back from this.

25:47.505 --> 25:50.758
You can't touch the Sun
and then come back down to Earth again.

25:51.759 --> 25:52.969
This life, uh...

25:54.053 --> 25:55.387
...it's got no taste now.

25:55.388 --> 25:57.138
It's got no feel.

25:57.139 --> 26:00.558
- Without you--
- But I'm right here.

26:00.559 --> 26:02.185
I'm standing right in front of you.

26:02.186 --> 26:03.603
And I'm long gone.

26:03.604 --> 26:05.314
We went to the doctor's lab.

26:06.315 --> 26:07.775
We saw the truth.

26:08.776 --> 26:10.485
There's no way out.
There was never gonna be a way out.

26:10.486 --> 26:11.654
You don't know that.

26:12.697 --> 26:14.614
- Listen, you--
- Stop.

26:14.615 --> 26:16.366
I don't care if I die.

26:16.367 --> 26:19.119
-  No...
- That's not what hurt me.

26:19.120 --> 26:21.246
What hurt me
is that you couldn't even wait

26:21.247 --> 26:24.500
for the dirt to hit my casket before
you went off with that private dick.

26:26.002 --> 26:27.502
You took him to the old theater.

26:29.547 --> 26:31.757
Where I saw you for the very first time.

26:32.383 --> 26:33.884
Wearing this very dress.

26:35.177 --> 26:36.470
Yeah.

26:44.937 --> 26:47.647
I ain't gonna tell Silvermane.

26:47.648 --> 26:49.065
But he's smart.

26:49.066 --> 26:51.444
He's gonna find out
what you did eventually.

26:52.903 --> 26:54.989
And I can't protect you when I'm dead.

27:06.917 --> 27:09.919
I'll have to stick them all.

27:09.920 --> 27:13.006
Once they're free and clear,
it'll be my turn.

27:13.007 --> 27:14.215
Well, that's a plan.

27:14.216 --> 27:15.884
Yeah, a terrible plan.

27:15.885 --> 27:18.303
Thanks for the confidence.
I think it's a great plan.

27:18.304 --> 27:20.013
Well, what do you want us to say?

27:20.014 --> 27:23.476
Nothing. I just want you to know
that this is the end of the story.

27:24.477 --> 27:26.311
No more sick veterans,

27:26.312 --> 27:28.189
no more suffering...

27:31.192 --> 27:32.860
...no more Spider.

27:37.573 --> 27:38.783
You've thought this over?

27:41.660 --> 27:44.246
For a long time.

27:45.831 --> 27:47.374
You're a good man, Ben Reilly.

27:47.375 --> 27:49.209
- Ha.
- You are.

27:49.210 --> 27:51.294
Look at you, you're helping people again.

27:51.295 --> 27:53.546
That's not why I'm doing it.

27:53.547 --> 27:55.007
Then why are you?

27:57.843 --> 28:00.595
Because with no power

28:00.596 --> 28:02.472
comes no responsibility.

28:02.473 --> 28:03.681
Ladies
and gentlemen,

28:03.682 --> 28:05.266
we have more breaking news to report.

28:05.267 --> 28:08.061
We have just learned
that the Silvermane gang is still at it,

28:08.062 --> 28:10.563
this time in Harlem,
where they've been seen pillaging

28:10.564 --> 28:13.733
a police warehouse,
stealing back all the confiscated hooch

28:13.734 --> 28:16.152
from Morris's big sting operation,

28:16.153 --> 28:18.530
and the cops are standing around
doing nothing.

28:18.531 --> 28:21.074
Who's in charge of the city, Mr. Morris?

28:21.075 --> 28:22.743
Harlem.

28:23.369 --> 28:25.370
Say, do me a favor.

28:25.371 --> 28:29.541
Just let me talk to him
before you swoop in and make it a fight.

28:29.542 --> 28:32.628
You think I want to fight?
Look at me. Wrong.

28:35.673 --> 28:38.634
Take a bottle on your way out,
and vote for Hudson.

28:40.302 --> 28:42.053
- Vote for Hudson.
- From Silvermane.

28:42.054 --> 28:43.471
Vote for Hudson.

28:43.472 --> 28:44.931
Hey, vote for Hudson.

28:46.434 --> 28:48.226
- Okay, sure.
- Vote for Hudson.

28:48.227 --> 28:49.602
Thanks, man.

28:49.603 --> 28:50.979
- Hi.
- You're welcome.

28:50.980 --> 28:52.522
- From Silvermane.
- Oh, what, are you a child?

28:52.523 --> 28:54.232
Take it. Take it.

28:54.233 --> 28:56.192
Go. Go, yeah.

28:56.193 --> 28:57.902
Just get out of here.

28:57.903 --> 28:58.946
Lonnie.

28:59.780 --> 29:01.990
- I just want to talk.
- Save your breath.

29:01.991 --> 29:04.535
I've picked my side.
This is how it is now.

29:05.536 --> 29:06.744
But why?

29:06.745 --> 29:08.164
What are you getting from all this?

29:09.373 --> 29:12.208
A soft bed, hot meals.

29:12.209 --> 29:14.419
More than I've had in a long time.

29:14.420 --> 29:16.838
And since I ain't got much of that left,

29:16.839 --> 29:18.882
I'm gonna enjoy whatever it is I do have.

29:18.883 --> 29:20.884
Come on, Lonnie.

29:20.885 --> 29:22.928
Come on, man,
I know you better than this, brother.

29:24.263 --> 29:25.680
- This ain't--
- Back off!

29:28.184 --> 29:29.976
Whatever your angle is,

29:29.977 --> 29:30.894
I--

29:35.065 --> 29:38.193
Lonnie,
Robbie's just trying to help you.

29:38.194 --> 29:40.320
I'm trying to help you, too.

29:40.321 --> 29:42.572
This doesn't have to be a fight.

29:42.573 --> 29:44.782
Well, it's gonna be.

29:44.783 --> 29:46.994
Okay,
not the response I was looking for.

30:05.888 --> 30:07.263
You trying to hurt me?

30:07.264 --> 30:09.265
You should know I live for the pain.

30:09.266 --> 30:10.476
I eat it up.

30:33.415 --> 30:34.917
Uh-oh.

30:41.882 --> 30:43.967
Whoa!

31:04.572 --> 31:06.407
You should've just let me be.

31:13.539 --> 31:15.165
Hey. Hey.

31:16.375 --> 31:18.836
Reilly? Hey.

31:23.424 --> 31:24.757
Where am I?

31:29.096 --> 31:31.098
Are you seeing this?

31:34.768 --> 31:36.312
You're not so tough now, are you?

31:44.111 --> 31:45.945
Oh, no, no. No, not now.

31:45.946 --> 31:47.489
Come on, come on.

32:01.712 --> 32:03.421
Get in.

32:03.422 --> 32:05.381
-  Stop them! Don't let them get out!
- Come on. Let's go, let's go,

32:05.382 --> 32:07.176
let's go, let's go.

32:10.971 --> 32:12.389
Hey!

32:17.561 --> 32:18.979
My car!

32:26.904 --> 32:29.364
Want to know why I'm helping you out?

32:29.365 --> 32:30.782
Mm-hmm.

32:30.783 --> 32:32.034
I owed you one.

32:33.035 --> 32:34.535
Now we're even.

32:37.581 --> 32:39.083
What about him?

32:40.084 --> 32:43.127
We don't have time
to get into all that.

32:43.128 --> 32:45.464
We got to ditch the car
and get him somewhere safe.

32:46.090 --> 32:47.925
We'll take him back to my place.

33:12.032 --> 33:13.700
Shouldn't we get him a doctor?

33:14.910 --> 33:16.619
Or a priest?

33:16.620 --> 33:18.037
Nah.

33:18.038 --> 33:19.581
He just needs to rest.

33:24.336 --> 33:26.212
Oh, no, are we still fighting?

33:26.213 --> 33:28.090
Nah. We're good.

33:28.674 --> 33:30.258
What-what's happening?

33:30.259 --> 33:32.552
We are at my place.

33:32.553 --> 33:35.054
You need to rest.

33:35.055 --> 33:36.639
I-I can't.

33:36.640 --> 33:38.725
I need to rest.

33:40.602 --> 33:41.812
Who is he?

33:45.899 --> 33:48.151
He's just a guy.

33:48.152 --> 33:50.361
Why'd he do it?

33:50.362 --> 33:52.531
Why'd he risk his life trying to help me?

33:53.991 --> 33:56.033
He was trying to save me.

33:56.034 --> 33:57.453
I almost killed him.

33:58.370 --> 34:02.082
Because, despite what he wants
everyone to believe...

34:03.208 --> 34:05.084
...he's a good person.

34:18.640 --> 34:21.059
- The hell is that?
- I don't know.

34:22.144 --> 34:24.146
But I know who's gonna want to know.

34:30.611 --> 34:32.613
Son of a bitch.

34:35.699 --> 34:37.201
Ah, shit.

34:39.161 --> 34:40.703
Mr. Mayor?

34:40.704 --> 34:42.205
The police chief is on his way.

34:42.206 --> 34:43.623
He's got news.

34:43.624 --> 34:45.125
Who cares?

34:47.503 --> 34:49.212
So,

34:49.213 --> 34:50.798
where you gonna go?

34:51.799 --> 34:53.424
I don't know.

34:54.968 --> 34:56.887
My mom's always wanted
to see Niagara Falls.

34:57.805 --> 34:59.222
Sounds as good a place as any.

34:59.223 --> 35:00.932
- Mm-hmm.
- You like maple syrup?

35:00.933 --> 35:02.809
As much as the next guy.

35:02.810 --> 35:04.561
Yeah...

35:05.854 --> 35:07.355
So, listen, um,

35:07.356 --> 35:09.566
- I wish I could do more--
- I'm good.

35:11.068 --> 35:12.778
Yes, you are.

35:17.574 --> 35:18.783
We're good.

35:20.202 --> 35:21.870
Everything you done for me...

35:22.955 --> 35:24.790
...not a lot of guys would've
went through the trouble.

35:26.333 --> 35:28.877
And everything you did
to get your job back at the Bugle?

35:29.878 --> 35:31.755
I hope they understand what you're worth.

35:33.465 --> 35:36.092
This city needs men like you

35:36.093 --> 35:38.011
just as much as it needs a guy like him.

35:40.931 --> 35:42.349
Brother.

35:43.642 --> 35:45.060
My man.

36:34.109 --> 36:35.526
When?

36:35.527 --> 36:37.445
A few hours ago.

36:37.446 --> 36:38.654
Which one?

36:38.655 --> 36:41.032
Lonnie Lincoln.

36:41.033 --> 36:42.491
Is this true?

36:42.492 --> 36:44.744
- We lost Lonnie?
-  That's right.

36:44.745 --> 36:47.080
We seen it with our own four eyes.

36:47.873 --> 36:48.999
How?

36:49.625 --> 36:52.501
The Spider showed up out of nowhere.

36:52.502 --> 36:54.086
- The Spider was there?
- The Spider?

36:54.087 --> 36:56.923
Lonnie was gonna kill him dead
until that reporter jumped in

36:56.924 --> 36:58.299
and jabbed him with something.

36:59.843 --> 37:01.803
- Jabbed him with what?
- Ah...

37:02.888 --> 37:06.141
Have some goddamn specificity
when you talk to me.

37:07.768 --> 37:09.519
He stuck him with one of these.

37:10.938 --> 37:12.647
Right in the eye.

37:12.648 --> 37:15.358
Whatever it is,
it brought the big fella down.

37:15.359 --> 37:18.277
Had him on his hands and knees,
sobbing like a baby.

37:18.278 --> 37:21.572
Raze out the written troubles
of the brain,

37:21.573 --> 37:24.618
and with some sweet oblivious antidote...

37:26.244 --> 37:28.746
...cleanse the stuffed bosom

37:28.747 --> 37:31.582
of that perilous stuff

37:31.583 --> 37:34.002
which weighs upon the heart.

37:36.213 --> 37:39.715
Looks like the good doctor
wasn't so crazy after all.

37:39.716 --> 37:43.219
So, Faber managed to give
some of that stuff to The Spider.

37:43.220 --> 37:45.513
Well, what are we gonna do, boss?

37:47.891 --> 37:49.350
What are you thinking?

37:49.351 --> 37:51.602
I'll tell you what we're gonna do.

37:51.603 --> 37:54.563
We are gonna find The Spider.

37:54.564 --> 37:56.566
- Get me Ben Reilly.
- Get me Ben Reilly.
